config.prompt:
You are preparing a list of tech companies for downstream market research.

The user provided three company names:
1. {{ inputs.company1 }}
2. {{ inputs.company2 }}
3. {{ inputs.company3 }}

Return the three companies as an ordered list, preserving the input order. Trim leading/trailing whitespace, expand obvious abbreviations only when unambiguous (e.g., 'GOOG' -> 'Google'), and otherwise keep the names exactly as provided. Do not add any companies the user did not list.

You are a strategy consultant maintaining a running comparative analysis of tech companies. On each loop iteration you fold one freshly-researched company into the running summary.

=== RUNNING SUMMARY FROM PREVIOUS ITERATIONS (empty on the first iteration) ===

Executive Summary so far:
{{ results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() > 1 ? results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations[results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() - 2].node-GX1q6qUq.output.data.executive_summary : null }}

Comparison Table so far:
{{ results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() > 1 ? results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations[results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() - 2].node-GX1q6qUq.output.data.comparison_table_markdown : null }}

Key Themes so far:
{{ results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() > 1 ? results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations[results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() - 2].node-GX1q6qUq.output.data.key_themes : null }}

Strategic Insights so far:
{{ results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() > 1 ? results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations[results.node-UHYq12DQ.iterations.size() - 2].node-GX1q6qUq.output.data.strategic_insights : null }}

=== NEW COMPANY RESEARCH (just produced this iteration) ===

Company Name: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.company_name }}
Business Overview: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.business_overview }}
Key Products/Services: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.key_products_services }}
Recent Developments: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.recent_developments }}
Market Position: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.market_position }}
Competitive Strengths: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.competitive_strengths }}
Challenges/Risks: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.key_challenges_risks }}
Future Outlook: {{ results.node-tQ_9Ygx6.output.data.future_outlook }}

=== TASK ===

Produce an UPDATED running summary that includes the new company alongside any companies already covered in the prior summary. If the prior summary is empty (first iteration), produce an initial summary covering only the new company.

Return these four fields:

1. executive_summary: 4-6 sentence narrative comparing all companies covered so far - what each is best known for, how they differ, and the most important takeaway.

2. comparison_table_markdown: A Markdown table with one row per company covered so far, columns: Company | Core Focus | Primary Customers | Notable Strength | Notable Risk. Keep cells to short phrases. Include the new company as a new row.

3. key_themes: A 3-5 bullet list (use '- ' prefix on each line) of cross-cutting themes across all companies covered so far. Refresh themes to reflect the newly added company.

4. strategic_insights: 4-6 sentence forward-looking analysis: where each company is likely heading, who is best positioned for the next 12-24 months, and why.

Be concrete and analytical. Do not invent facts not present in the research above or in the prior summary.

